A||N||7||x-thumpr-x|| PFF members of Ontario & Guests||||1||
Z||000000||x-thumpr-x||10-09-2001||04:02 PM||||How many PFF members are from ontario (canada) and who belongs to the GTA club?<P>Respectively, what is your opinion on the club and how can it be improved or does it need to be? (please refrain from lashing out at other members of the club and sponsers)<P>I am a recently new member and would like to see the club grow in numbers. I took my first trip this summer with the GTA club to FrankenMuth for the Michigan Fiero Show and waz amazed at all the cars there and the community this car has formed.<P>I have seen alot of fieros in the GTA & surrounding area  but lately I've come to understand the GTA club has some internal  "Bickering" which might be defacing the GTA club and what it's members & non memebers think of it. Though it still has a strong backbone,  the club needs it's members to keep it afloat. I would like to see the club progress through this to keep another part of the "Community " alive.<P>Has any other club encountered this before and how did you survive?<P>This is not intended to harm any member of the club or sponser(s). More so of a way to ask others what we can do to make it a better club for our members and future members.||||reg||1
Z||000001||x-thumpr-x||10-09-2001||09:15 PM||||bump||||reg||1
Z||000002||grinthock||10-09-2001||09:51 PM||||Well I guess I was destined to respond eventually.<P>I see many problems with the GTA club.<P>First, the outside opinions I hear of the GTA clubs are not good.  They HAD a great reputation of being a good club, still do for most part.<P>The club needs to completly REMOVE itself from it's primary sponsor.  The club itself was owned/operated basically BY the primary sponsor.  Anyone who did not like the primary sponsor, or anyone who doesn't get along with them was not welcome.<P>Some of the club executives (and as you requested I will not use names) are not running the club properly, biased against certain fiero owners, asking people not to attend and "thretening" them.<P>The people in the club for the most part like the club and want it to succeed but then when it's time to ACT they don't want to get involved. ONE person can not run the club, ONE person can not do a newsletter or be the organizer of a cruise.<P>The club is now a Clic.  And I am not the only one to say this.  It's a clic of people like in high school if you are not liked then you are gone.  This is the single biggest problem.<P>The club has a chance, but it needs changes<P>My view.  Anyone else care to comment or are you all going to sit in your trenches and hide from the truth that you ALL know just like last time they lashed at me?<P>I am not afriad to state my views as the club all knows, they say I bad mouth the club because of the comments I make here.  Bad mouth?  No.  Only truth telling.<P>I could start naming names of people who agree with me, but I will let them sit and hide and just ride along and "not create waves" as they usually do.<BR><P>------------------<BR> <A HREF="http://www.fieroworld.com" TARGET=_blank> <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/fieroworldbanner.gif"> </A> <BR>Fieroworld!  Home of my 87 GT and 85 GT<BR>Justin C.<BR>Engineer, Designer and<BR>Technical Trainer for Nortel Networks Business Products.||||reg||1
Z||000003||banditbalz||10-09-2001||10:27 PM||||I am a current member of the GTA club. I haven't been to a meeting in 6 months (they are an hour away), so I may not be entitled to speak. I agree on the most part as to Grinthock's post. I can see his frustration in being ostricized by the primary sponser. The views of the sponser tend to spill into the club population and the next thing you know, you're not welcome anymore.<P>On another note, I found the meetings a little "dry" at times. I think we need to inject more energy into the meetings and  get guys excited about driving their cars again. Instead of planning picnics, I would like to see organized autoX or a dragrace event. These are sportscars we are driving, not SUV's.<BR>I'm not sure if removing the primary sponser is going to be an advantage. I will continue to use their services and support them for the simple fact they know Fieros. And let's face it, who else can you trust your car too?<P><BR> <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/blackwhite2_1.jpg"> <P><P>------------------<BR>Silver 86 GT<BR>completely stock,<BR>completely fast!||||reg||3
Z||000004||grinthock||10-09-2001||10:34 PM||||I have to agree with bandit, my personal tiff with their primary sponsor IS what tossed me.  But that's not appropriate here to get into.  I had a problem with them.  That's all I will say.<P><BR>Bandit is right, the club meetings were BORING, we sat there and did nothing except talk about where we were going after the meeting.  If they planned events, cruises, TECH DAYS (hint hint nudge nudge), road rallys, get togeathers, autoX would be GREAT, as well as drag days, not just dragging AFTER the meetings.  There is drag days now, but they only call 4-5 close nit members and that's all.<P>Thanks BanditBalz for being the first to come out of the closet, I only pray you are not ostricized.||||reg||1
Z||000005||FieroBUZZ||10-10-2001||12:45 AM||||It seems in the Ottawa area clubs have died out. A couple have been advertised or promoted and prior to launch have fizzled.  <P>Maybe an imperfect club is better than none at all.  Maybe you can start a second club and challenge the other guys.  Then at least you get to race  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/biggrin.gif">  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/biggrin.gif"><BR> <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/buzzsig_7.jpg"> ||||reg||9
Z||000006||Tonker||10-10-2001||01:06 PM|||| <BLOCKQUOTE><font size="1" face="Verdana, Arial, Helvetica">quote:</font><HR>Originally posted by FieroBUZZ:<BR><B>It seems in the Ottawa area clubs have died out. A couple have been advertised or promoted and prior to launch have fizzled.  <BR></B><HR></BLOCKQUOTE><P>Does that mean I can come down and visit you guys to see what these clubs are all about?  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/frown.gif"><BR>||||reg||9
Z||000007||x-thumpr-x||10-10-2001||05:14 PM||||Thanks to the members who have repied so-far. I know there is more out there that would like to have a say. Since I'm new, I have no quorrels with any members or sponsers like other members or former members do I guess I can see things from a different angle. I think we can set aside differences of opinions and try to rebuild the club. The club does need it's members & sponsers to help keep it running and yes, each individual has a prefference of shop, or parts source, All I say is keep personal queralls personal. <P>As for some of the ideas of actually getting activities going for the summer, I'm in on that. I'd like to see some actual outings and some Tech Days. This would help people (& myself!) learn more about there Fieros and help maintane them. To do this though, we need a major turnout for the club meeting and seriously discuss some options. Then get volunteers to look into them. <P>The next meeting will be Oct. 16  7pm at the Happy Greek. Located on steeeles just east of Keele. (pass under train tracks and take a left @ first lights)<BR>Lets see how many we can get to show up for this meeting. ||||reg||1
